                            <td class="state">not implemented</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <p class="note">Studio means the shell reacts to host replies. It does not mean a workbook was read.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Format honesty</h2>
            </div>
            <p>
                A recognized extension only means the product can classify the
                file. What this build actually reads, writes or inspects is
                reported by the capability matrix, per format. While the engine
                is absent, every domain operation reports
                <code>capability/not-implemented</code> instead of returning a
                partial workbook.
            </p>
            <p class="note">
                Declared formats: <code>xlsx</code>, <code>xlsm</code>,
                <code>xltx</code>, <code>xls</code>, <code>csv</code>,
                <code>tsv</code>, <code>ods</code>, <code>json</code>,
                <code>xml</code> and <code>pdf</code>. A suffix is not a
                support claim.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Current state</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="state-row">
                <span class="chip chip--mono">workbook.create</span>
                <span class="chip chip--mono">workbook.open</span>
                <span class="chip chip--mono">workbook.save</span>
                <span class="chip chip--mono">workbook.inspect</span>
                <span class="chip chip--mono">workbook.export</span>
                <span class="chip chip--mono">workbook.close</span>
            </div>
            <p class="note">
                Every one of these calls rejects with
                <code>capability/not-implemented</code>. The studio surfaces the
                error in its diagnostics tab and leaves the sheet empty.
            </p>
        </section>

